# omageeko package map: upstream install/omarchy-base.packages -> Tumbleweed
# Format: <arch-name> <layer> <tw-packages,comma,separated | @build | @flatpak:<id> | @repo:<alias> | -> [# note]
#   layer  = omageeko layer that installs it (01 base, 02 build, 04 session, 05 shell, 06 login-boot, 07 system, 08 apps)
#   @build = RPM built from packages/<name> (@build:<rpm> when the RPM name differs from the Arch name)
#   -      = intentionally skipped (reason in note); a "-" layer with a real target is
#            not installed by any layer but still translated for omarchy-pkg-add
# Lines whose name starts with '+' are omageeko extras (not in upstream's list).
# Every package in upstream's list must appear here; layers/01-base-packages/verify.sh checks that.

